{"kind": "intervention", "cursor": 63, "request_id": "97fd1caca7a949358ace1a740316939d", "message": "Target 4 (thrift codec fallback) implementation is incorrect. The requirement states: \"codec fails when CodecType is Basic and message type does not support Apache codec\" - meaning typecodec.Apache=False.\n\nYour current fix adds error-based fallback INSIDE the \"if typecodec.Apache\" block. But when typecodec.Apache=False, that entire block is SKIPPED, so your fallback never executes.\n\n**Test case that still fails:**\n- CodecType = Basic\n- typecodec.Apache = false (message doesn't support Apache)\n- typecodec.FastCodec = true (message supports FastCodec)\n\nCode flow: Skip FrugalWrite check → Skip FastWrite check → Skip \"if typecodec.Apache\" block → Skip \"if c.CodecType != Basic\" block → Return errEncodeMismatchMsgType ❌\n\n**Correct fix in marshalThriftData (line ~82):**\nChange `if c.CodecType != Basic {` to just remove the condition:\n```go\n// try fallback to frugal or fastcodec for all codec types\nif typecodec.FastCodec {\n    return fastMarshalData(data)\n}\nif typecodec.Frugal {\n    return frugalMarshalData(data)\n}\n```\n\nSame fix needed in unmarshalThriftData (line ~154). The error-based fallback you added can stay as defensive code, but the main fix is removing the \"!= Basic\" restriction.", "delivery": "handed_to_task_interrupt_interface", "receipt": "InterruptionRequest(sequence=2, message='Target 4 (thrift codec fallback) implementation is incorrect. The requirement states: \"codec fails when CodecType is Basic and message type does not support Apache codec\" - meaning typecodec.Apache=False.\\n\\nYour current fix adds error-based fallback INSIDE the \"if typecodec.Apache\" block. But when typecodec.Apache=False, that entire block is SKIPPED, so your fallback never executes.\\n\\n**Test case that still fails:**\\n- CodecType = Basic\\n- typecodec.Apache = false (message doesn\\'t support Apache)\\n- typecodec.FastCodec = true (message supports FastCodec)\\n\\nCode flow: Skip FrugalWrite check → Skip FastWrite check → Skip \"if typecodec.Apache\" block → Skip \"if c.CodecType != Basic\" block → Return errEncodeMismatchMsgType ❌\\n\\n**Correct fix in marshalThriftData (line ~82):**\\nChange `if c.CodecType != Basic {` to just remove the condition:\\n```go\\n// try fallback to frugal or fastcodec for all codec types\\nif typecodec.FastCodec {\\n    return fastMarshalData(data)\\n}\\nif typecodec.Frugal {\\n    return frugalMarshalData(data)\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSame fix needed in unmarshalThriftData (line ~154). The error-based fallback you added can stay as defensive code, but the main fix is removing the \"!= Basic\" restriction.', source='monitor', created_at=1791207483.1004446)", "resumed_completion_requests": []}
